      "key" : "abstract",
      "lastUpdateTs" : 1784970494712,
      "longValue" : null,
      "strValue" : "A UNESCO project to strengthen Ghana’s resilience against floods and droughts to protect lives and livelihoods with the support of the Government of Japan."
    }, {
      "booleanValue" : null,
      "doubleValue" : null,
      "jsonValue" : null,
      "key" : "description",
      "lastUpdateTs" : 1784970755166,
      "longValue" : null,
      "strValue" : "<p>UNESCO, in partnership with the Government of Ghana and with financial support from Japan, has launched a 12-month project to strengthen resilience to floods and droughts under climate change in Ghana. The project <it>\"Strengthening Resilience on Water-Related Disasters under Climate Change for a Sustainable Society in Ghana’’</it> combines scientific innovation, local community empowerment, and policy support to address the root causes of water-related disasters.</p><p>Focusing on the Volta River Basin and other high-risk areas, the initiative provides input for national adaptation planning while equipping communities with practical tools to reduce risks and safeguard livelihoods.</p><p>See also: <a href=\"https://www.unesco.org/en/articles/strengthening-resilience-water-related-disasters-ghana\">press release</a></p>"
    }, {
      "booleanValue" : null,
      "doubleValue" : null,
      "jsonValue" : null,
      "key" : "title",
      "lastUpdateTs" : 1784970450988,
      "longValue" : null,
      "strValue" : "Strengthening resilience to water-related disasters in Ghana"
    } ]
